content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-201 - Velatek VX-90 dosing pump, serial VX-5531 (diaphragm leaking chemical at the head)",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Diaphragm leakage at the head of about 2 drops per second: no documented limit applies. None of the evidence covers the Velatek VX-90. The only manufacturer data supplied is for the AquaDyne HF-300 centrifugal pump, which does not apply to this asset. The leak cannot be compared against a manufacturer limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Motor running normally: no motor limits for the VX-90 are in the evidence. The HF-300 motor data (55 kW, 1480 rpm) and bearing temperature limits (alarm 80 C, trip 90 C) belong to a different pump and do not apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No vibration or bearing temperature readings were reported. The site triggers for stopping the machine (vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone) and for a P1 work order (bearing temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit) are therefore not met. The HF-300 vibration zones in Figure 3 do not apply to the VX-90.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Priority P2 is a planning judgement and is not mandated by any document. No site rule forces P1 or an immediate stop for this symptom, but an active chemical leak needs prompt planned repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for all work on and around the leaking dosing head, including the initial inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump head or diaphragm, electrically isolate the pump and apply lock-out/tag-out (LOTO) at the MCC.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves of P-201.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Obtain a line-break permit, then drain and vent the dosing head and lines before breaking into the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect and replace the diaphragm following the Velatek VX-90 manufacturer procedure. That procedure, its torque values and its part numbers are not in the supplied evidence and must be obtained before work starts. Do not use AquaDyne HF-300 procedures or torques (Table 5 or SB-2026-014).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "SSP-07 applies to all pumps on site, so it applies to P-201. The work order must list every applicable control.",
      "citations": [
        "C14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Work inside the pump: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC; mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves; line-break permit (drain and vent first).",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Work on chemically dosed lines: chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. The pump is reported to be leaking chemical, so this control applies.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting plan and certified lifting equipment are required only if any component exceeds 25 kg. The VX-90 component masses are not in the evidence; confirm before work.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The AquaDyne HF-300 O&M manual (parts list, procedures, Table 5 torques, troubleshooting, vibration zones, temperature limits) does not apply. P-201 is a Velatek VX-90 dosing pump, serial VX-5531, not an AquaDyne HF-300.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The manual's Table 5 (seal gland nut 25 Nm, seal HF3-450) disagrees with Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (cartridge seal HF3-450B at 30 Nm for serials HF3-22000 and above). Neither applies to this asset: serial VX-5531 is not in the HF3 serial range, and P-201 has a diaphragm, not a mechanical seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "SSP-07 names P-101 to P-106 as the chemically dosed (sodium hypochlorite) pumps; P-201 is not listed. The fault report states P-201 is leaking chemical, so the chemically dosed line controls are applied. SSP-07 itself applies to all site pumps.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What chemical is P-201 dosing, and what is its safety data sheet? C16 only identifies sodium hypochlorite on P-101 to P-106, and additional PPE or spill containment may be needed.",
    "What is the Velatek VX-90 acceptable diaphragm leakage limit, and should the pump be stopped immediately to contain the leak? No VX-90 documentation was provided.",
    "What are the probable causes of diaphragm leakage on the VX-90 (e.g. diaphragm rupture or fatigue, head bolt loosening, overpressure)? The only troubleshooting table supplied is for the HF-300.",
    "What is the VX-90 diaphragm replacement procedure, including head bolt torque values?",
    "What are the VX-90 spare part numbers and quantities (diaphragm, head seals or O-rings, valves)?",
    "What are the component masses (to confirm whether the >25 kg lifting control applies)?",
    "What labour is required (trades, headcount, duration)? No labour data is in the evidence.",
    "Is a standby dosing pump available to maintain treatment while P-201 is isolated?"
  ]
}
